{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRytRoNkUCPjiLhLiGZc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job failed on every run (6 so far) for two reasons, and the second one hid the first. I fixed the script bug but not the login problem, so the job still won't produce a summary yet. I haven't run anything. The edits are in the snapshot only, and the causes are written up in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n1. **`claude` isn't logged in when launchd runs it.** `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err` shows `Not logged in · Please run /login` on every run, so `claude -p` exits non-zero and there is never a summary.\n   - **Your step:** run `claude setup-token` in a terminal and add the token to the plist's `EnvironmentVariables` as `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`. An `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` would also work. Then reload the agent. I didn't add a token myself.\n\n2. **The failure note could never be sent.** In `bin/nightly-review.zsh`, `status=$?` fails in zsh with `read-only variable: status`, because `$status` is a built-in alias of `$?`. The script died there, so `notify.sh` was never called. That is why you didn't even get a failure message. I renamed the variable to `rc`.\n\nI also added `--fail` to the `curl` call in `bin/notify.sh`. Without it, a Telegram error such as a bad token or wrong chat id would be swallowed silently. That wasn't one of the causes.\n\nOnce the token is in place, `launchctl kickstart gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review` will run the job right away. After that, check Telegram and the `.err` log."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":457,"cache_read_input_tokens":24653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":457},"output_tokens":530,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_